<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="0.16" dur="4.24">Please welcome to the stage the Attorney</text><text start="2.24" dur="5.16">General of the United States, Todd</text><text start="4.4" dur="3">Blanch.</text><text start="10.48" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="15.839" dur="3.241">Thank you.</text><text start="19.119" dur="4.08">Thank you. Good afternoon.</text><text start="21.68" dur="4.24">Welcome to the Department of Justice.</text><text start="23.199" dur="5.041">And I want to be the first to welcome uh</text><text start="25.92" dur="4.32">President Trump to his second trip back</text><text start="28.24" dur="3.839">to the Department of Justice as a 47th</text><text start="30.24" dur="4.56">President of the United States. We are</text><text start="32.079" dur="4.961">honored, humbled, and thrilled to have</text><text start="34.8" dur="4.4">you join us today, Mr. President. And on</text><text start="37.04" dur="4.4">behalf of the prosecutors in the room,</text><text start="39.2" dur="5.199">the law enforcement members in the room,</text><text start="41.44" dur="4.959">and everybody that&amp;#39;s here today, let me</text><text start="44.399" dur="4.561">just tell you that we are here. We are</text><text start="46.399" dur="4.401">so appreciative that President Trump</text><text start="48.96" dur="4.4">delivered on his promise to the American</text><text start="50.8" dur="4.32">people that when he took office again</text><text start="53.36" dur="4.64">that he would do everything in his power</text><text start="55.12" dur="6.4">to unleash law enforcement to do their</text><text start="58" dur="5.199">jobs to keep this country safe again,</text><text start="61.52" dur="4.4">which is exactly what he&amp;#39;s done. So,</text><text start="63.199" dur="6.041">thank you, Mr. President. We&amp;#39;re also on</text><text start="65.92" dur="3.32">Thank you.</text><text start="69.28" dur="5.92">We&amp;#39;re also honored to welcome some of</text><text start="72.479" dur="4.64">the families of the victims whose lives</text><text start="75.2" dur="5.68">were forever changed by the vicious</text><text start="77.119" dur="6.401">behavior of the death row inmates whose</text><text start="80.88" dur="5.36">sentences have now been commuted by</text><text start="83.52" dur="5.52">Governor Nuome. Thank you very much for</text><text start="86.24" dur="7.6">being here today and thank you for</text><text start="89.04" dur="7.039">speaking up. Mr. President, on day one,</text><text start="93.84" dur="4.4">on day one of your presidency, you</text><text start="96.079" dur="4.321">issued an executive order that directed</text><text start="98.24" dur="5.6">the Department of Justice to seek the</text><text start="100.4" dur="6.24">death penalty wherever appropriate.</text><text start="103.84" dur="6.08">Since January 20th of last year, the</text><text start="106.64" dur="6.64">Department of Justice has done so 49</text><text start="109.92" dur="5.6">times. Now, when you compare that to the</text><text start="113.28" dur="4.4">last administration, during the last</text><text start="115.52" dur="4.72">administration, the Department of</text><text start="117.68" dur="4.399">Justice sought the death penalty one</text><text start="120.24" dur="5.36">time.</text><text start="122.079" dur="5.601">One time. That is not justice. That is</text><text start="125.6" dur="3.999">not what the American people deserve.</text><text start="127.68" dur="4.559">That is not what the families of victims</text><text start="129.599" dur="4.481">of horrific murders deserve. And so, Mr.</text><text start="132.239" dur="3.36">President, I assure you that this</text><text start="134.08" dur="4.32">Department of Justice is seeking the</text><text start="135.599" dur="5.681">death penalty whenever appropriate for</text><text start="138.4" dur="5.12">crimes get committed in this country.</text><text start="141.28" dur="4.959">So,</text><text start="143.52" dur="4.64">I want to take just a moment</text><text start="146.239" dur="4.481">and tell every law enforcement member</text><text start="148.16" dur="4.719">watching or here in this room that we</text><text start="150.72" dur="4.159">have your back, that President Trump has</text><text start="152.879" dur="5.761">your back, and he will always have your</text><text start="154.879" dur="5.521">back. to the families</text><text start="158.64" dur="4.8">to the families of the victims of the</text><text start="160.4" dur="4.88">horrible crimes that have been committed</text><text start="163.44" dur="4.64">not only in California but around this</text><text start="165.28" dur="5.28">country. Make no mistake about it that</text><text start="168.08" dur="4.4">this Department of Justice every single</text><text start="170.56" dur="5.039">day that our prosecutors that our</text><text start="172.48" dur="6.32">federal agents will do everything we can</text><text start="175.599" dur="5.761">to impose the harshest penalty possible</text><text start="178.8" dur="4.4">under the facts of the case consistent</text><text start="181.36" dur="4">with the president&amp;#39;s agenda. That&amp;#39;s what</text><text start="183.2" dur="4.64">we have done since January 20th. of what</text><text start="185.36" dur="6.879">we will continue to do from this day</text><text start="187.84" dur="6.8">going forward. So with that, let me be</text><text start="192.239" dur="6.161">um let me just ask everybody to get on</text><text start="194.64" dur="5.44">their feet and welcome the 45th and 47th</text><text start="198.4" dur="4.652">president of the United States,</text><text start="200.08" dur="4.992">President Donald J. Trump.</text><text start="203.052" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="211.567" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="219.44" dur="3.079">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Heat. Heat.</text><text start="231.872" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="237.112" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="241.697" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="246.319" dur="6.321">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you very much. Please. Thank you.</text><text start="249.519" dur="7.12">It&amp;#39;s a great honor.</text><text start="252.64" dur="7.68">I want to just welcome all of you to a</text><text start="256.639" dur="6.56">very safe Washington DC. You know, the</text><text start="260.32" dur="4.64">crime rates gone down 84%</text><text start="263.199" dur="4.641">and a lot of the people in this room are</text><text start="264.96" dur="6.56">responsible for that. And I want to</text><text start="267.84" dur="5.6">thank you to a very special thanks to an</text><text start="271.52" dur="3.36">outstanding attorney general. It&amp;#39;s going</text><text start="273.44" dur="2.96">to be one of the greats. I think he&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="274.88" dur="3.44">go down as one of the greats when we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="276.4" dur="5.32">finished. Todd Blanch. Thank you, Todd.</text><text start="278.32" dur="3.4">Appreciate it.</text><text start="283.84" dur="5.68">Where is he? What happened? He&amp;#39;s around.</text><text start="286.88" dur="4.96">He&amp;#39;s around here someplace. I can&amp;#39;t I</text><text start="289.52" dur="5.52">want to say hello to Todd. He&amp;#39;s special.</text><text start="291.84" dur="5.28">He works all the time. We&amp;#39;re here today</text><text start="295.04" dur="5.2">to talk about one of the most shocking</text><text start="297.12" dur="4.799">acts of injustice our country has ever</text><text start="300.24" dur="3.36">seen. I couldn&amp;#39;t believe it. I witnessed</text><text start="301.919" dur="4.161">it a couple of weeks ago. I couldn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="303.6" dur="5.599">believe it. Just days ago, the governor</text><text start="306.08" dur="6.72">of California, Gavin Nuome, granted</text><text start="309.199" dur="7.28">clemency and mercy to 548 of the most</text><text start="312.8" dur="6.72">evil monsters on the face of the earth.</text><text start="316.479" dur="5.601">You&amp;#39;d have to read their biographies to</text><text start="319.52" dur="3.92">see how bad they were. Some of them you</text><text start="322.08" dur="5.28">wouldn&amp;#39;t even believe it. All of them,</text><text start="323.44" dur="7.12">but some of them you would levels of</text><text start="327.36" dur="4.72">craziness, sickness that I&amp;#39;ve never seen</text><text start="330.56" dur="4.56">before.</text><text start="332.08" dur="6.72">Among those death row inmates he granted</text><text start="335.12" dur="6.16">clemency were more than 110 child</text><text start="338.8" dur="4.959">killers, more than 100 rapists who</text><text start="341.28" dur="4.16">murdered their victims, and numerous</text><text start="343.759" dur="4.801">serial killers who tortured and</text><text start="345.44" dur="4.96">slaughtered dozens of innocent people</text><text start="348.56" dur="3.44">at levels that nobody&amp;#39;s ever seen</text><text start="350.4" dur="5.359">before.</text><text start="352" dur="6.8">Among the serial killers he spared is</text><text start="355.759" dur="5.28">Charles Ing, who tortured, enslaved, and</text><text start="358.8" dur="4.8">slaughtered at least 11 people,</text><text start="361.039" dur="5.921">including babies, in a torture chamber</text><text start="363.6" dur="6.719">in a remote cabin, as well as the</text><text start="366.96" dur="6.72">Southside Slayer who killed 14 women and</text><text start="370.319" dur="6.961">enjoyed every moment of it in an unborn</text><text start="373.68" dur="5.76">child in South Los Angeles.</text><text start="377.28" dur="6.32">and the scorecard killer. They call him</text><text start="379.44" dur="6.64">the scorecard killer who kept a tally in</text><text start="383.6" dur="5.439">his car of at least 16 young men he</text><text start="386.08" dur="5.679">abducted, raped and murdered. And the</text><text start="389.039" dur="5.521">alphabet killer was that name, alphabet</text><text start="391.759" dur="5.761">killer, who raped and murdered innocent</text><text start="394.56" dur="5.68">young girls whose first and last name</text><text start="397.52" dur="6.239">started with the same letter. He needed</text><text start="400.24" dur="5.519">that same letter. These are sick people.</text><text start="403.759" dur="5.041">This afternoon, we come together to</text><text start="405.759" dur="5.121">stand against the travesty and to wrap</text><text start="408.8" dur="4.64">our arms around the families of victims</text><text start="410.88" dur="6.319">who were so cruy betrayed by bad</text><text start="413.44" dur="6.08">government and our political system. To</text><text start="417.199" dur="5.681">every parent, son, daughter, sibling, or</text><text start="419.52" dur="7.36">spouse here today whose loved one was</text><text start="422.88" dur="6.56">brutally killed by those monsters, we</text><text start="426.88" dur="6.64">love you. We support you and we are with</text><text start="429.44" dur="6.879">you and your quest for un really the the</text><text start="433.52" dur="4.799">ultimate of final justice. We have to do</text><text start="436.319" dur="3.681">this. We can&amp;#39;t let this happen. What</text><text start="438.319" dur="5.921">happened to you, what happened to all of</text><text start="440" dur="7.44">us should not be allowed to stand. What</text><text start="444.24" dur="6.079">these families have endured is beyond</text><text start="447.44" dur="5.759">imagination.</text><text start="450.319" dur="5.28">One day their lives were shattered into</text><text start="453.199" dur="4.881">pieces when they learned that someone</text><text start="455.599" dur="4.32">they had loved most in the entire world</text><text start="458.08" dur="4.959">they loved more than anybody in the</text><text start="459.919" dur="5.921">world had spent their final moments in</text><text start="463.039" dur="6.961">excruciating pain and bone chilling</text><text start="465.84" dur="7.28">terror and those families lives will</text><text start="470" dur="5.52">never ever be the same. Then after the</text><text start="473.12" dur="4.72">juries delivered their verdicts and the</text><text start="475.52" dur="5.04">justice system returned a muchdeserved</text><text start="477.84" dur="4.56">sentence of death,</text><text start="480.56" dur="3.84">Nuome,</text><text start="482.4" dur="5.04">a terrible governor in so many other</text><text start="484.4" dur="5.68">ways, came along and stole away the only</text><text start="487.44" dur="4.72">closure those families</text><text start="490.08" dur="4.239">might ever have.</text><text start="492.16" dur="5.2">He stood with the murderers and the</text><text start="494.319" dur="5.921">child slayers. But today, we say, the</text><text start="497.36" dur="4.32">American people, stand with you. We</text><text start="500.24" dur="4.72">stand with you. We&amp;#39;re not going to let</text><text start="501.68" dur="8.32">this happen.</text><text start="504.96" dur="8.4">In May 1996, 8-year-old Michael Lions</text><text start="510" dur="6.399">was walking home from elementary school</text><text start="513.36" dur="6.159">in Yuba City, California,</text><text start="516.399" dur="7.041">when he was abducted by convicted sex</text><text start="519.519" dur="6.241">offender Robert Boyd Rhodess, who forced</text><text start="523.44" dur="6.519">young Michael into a secluded area,</text><text start="525.76" dur="4.199">raped and tortured him</text><text start="530.32" dur="5.199">for extended periods of time. The</text><text start="533.519" dur="5.601">predators slashed Michael more than a</text><text start="535.519" dur="6.561">hundred times with a knife and left his</text><text start="539.12" dur="6.719">body on a river bank for others to pick</text><text start="542.08" dur="6.56">up. Roads was captured and sentenced to</text><text start="545.839" dur="5.201">death. But Gavin Newsome thought that</text><text start="548.64" dur="5.28">child killer was owed the mercy that he</text><text start="551.04" dur="5.28">never showed to 8-year-old</text><text start="553.92" dur="5.28">Michael. We&amp;#39;re joined by Michael&amp;#39;s</text><text start="556.32" dur="5.68">family, including his mother, Sandy. And</text><text start="559.2" dur="6.199">Sandy, I&amp;#39;d like to have you say a few</text><text start="562" dur="3.399">words, please.</text><text start="566.56" dur="5.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you.</text><text start="568.72" dur="3.32">Thank you, darling.</text><text start="572.24" dur="6.32">Hi, my name is Sandy Friend. I am the</text><text start="575.6" dur="5.6">mother of Michael Lions.</text><text start="578.56" dur="7.44">Michael was eight years old. He loved</text><text start="581.2" dur="7.759">his sisters, fishing ninja turtles,</text><text start="586" dur="6.24">telling campfire stories,</text><text start="588.959" dur="6.401">and bringing me flowers.</text><text start="592.24" dur="5.2">Michael was afraid of the dark. He</text><text start="595.36" dur="3.76">believed the boogeyman was going to get</text><text start="597.44" dur="6">him.</text><text start="599.12" dur="7.279">On May 16th, 1996, Robert Boyd Rhodess,</text><text start="603.44" dur="6.399">a twice convicted sex offender and</text><text start="606.399" dur="6.241">serial killer, kidnapped Michael.</text><text start="609.839" dur="6.56">Walking home from school, he took my</text><text start="612.64" dur="7.439">little boy into the darkness. His most</text><text start="616.399" dur="5.601">feared thing was the dark. That night,</text><text start="620.079" dur="4.921">Michael learned that the boogeyman was</text><text start="622" dur="3">real.</text><text start="626.88" dur="7.84">Mikey was raped, sodomized, and tortured</text><text start="630.72" dur="7.28">from 10 for 10 hours. From the very</text><text start="634.72" dur="5.52">first inflicted stabin</text><text start="638" dur="5.56">to the last,</text><text start="640.24" dur="3.32">he only</text><text start="646.64" dur="4.56">that is why the killer was convicted of</text><text start="649.44" dur="4.8">torture.</text><text start="651.2" dur="6.96">A jury sentenced him to die and in</text><text start="654.24" dur="9.282">December 2025 a judge reaffirmed that</text><text start="658.16" dur="6.4">sentence. The go the governor then sorry</text><text start="663.522" dur="4.798">[sighs]</text><text start="664.56" dur="6.959">this is so very hard. [gasps]</text><text start="668.32" dur="5.68">Then Governor Nome erased that with the</text><text start="671.519" dur="6.921">swipe of a pen</text><text start="674" dur="4.44">without notifying the families.</text><text start="678.8" dur="6.24">Governor Nuome,</text><text start="681.6" dur="7.6">we deserve to be heard.</text><text start="685.04" dur="6.96">You never heard what my child endured or</text><text start="689.2" dur="5.759">lived with the emptiness of having an</text><text start="692" dur="4.48">empty chair at every holiday and</text><text start="694.959" dur="5.041">milestone.</text><text start="696.48" dur="5.919">Yet you took the only justice we had and</text><text start="700" dur="5.2">left families feeling abandoned by the</text><text start="702.399" dur="5.68">state that promised to protect us.</text><text start="705.2" dur="5.28">You&amp;#39;ll never understand the unimaginable</text><text start="708.079" dur="6.561">pain that you&amp;#39;re putting these families</text><text start="710.48" dur="6.16">through. Face me, Governor Nuome. Tell</text><text start="714.64" dur="5.759">me, Michael&amp;#39;s</text><text start="716.64" dur="6.319">Michael&amp;#39;s life doesn&amp;#39;t matter.</text><text start="720.399" dur="5.201">Michael deserved a governor who who</text><text start="722.959" dur="5.44">would stand with the victims, honor</text><text start="725.6" dur="5.679">their justice, and respect the will of</text><text start="728.399" dur="5.601">the people. You may have taken our</text><text start="731.279" dur="5.601">justice, but we will never you will</text><text start="734" dur="5.04">never take Michael&amp;#39;s voice.</text><text start="736.88" dur="5.68">Mr. President, thank you for standing</text><text start="739.04" dur="6.56">with the victims and giving us a voice.</text><text start="742.56" dur="7.44">I will never stop speaking Michael&amp;#39;s</text><text start="745.6" dur="8.88">name. Every victim matters. Look at his</text><text start="750" dur="7.72">face. He was only eight years old.</text><text start="754.48" dur="3.24">Thank you.</text><text start="776.32" dur="5.36">Sandy, we will always be with you. And</text><text start="779.44" dur="4.72">you&amp;#39;re beautiful, Michael. And thank you</text><text start="781.68" dur="5.12">very much. It&amp;#39;s great bravery even to be</text><text start="784.16" dur="5.44">here because Todd and the whole group, a</text><text start="786.8" dur="5.039">lot of people in this room are working</text><text start="789.6" dur="5.28">as hard as they can to get this travesty</text><text start="791.839" dur="6.721">overturned in some form. Very unusual</text><text start="794.88" dur="7.04">situation. state. We&amp;#39;re we&amp;#39;re very</text><text start="798.56" dur="7.839">active doing everything we can. In</text><text start="801.92" dur="8.159">October 1993, 12-year-old Polyclass was</text><text start="806.399" dur="6.401">having a slumber party at her home in</text><text start="810.079" dur="6.56">Paluma, California, when a violent</text><text start="812.8" dur="8.88">repeat offender out of parole slipped</text><text start="816.639" dur="8.32">into her home carrying a large violent</text><text start="821.68" dur="6.159">knife. He bound and gagged Pauliey&amp;#39;s two</text><text start="824.959" dur="5.201">friends and abducted Polly. Two months</text><text start="827.839" dur="4.8">later, she was found buried in a very</text><text start="830.16" dur="6.239">shallow grave over 50 miles from her</text><text start="832.639" dur="6.64">home. Nuome gave Paulie&amp;#39;s savage killer</text><text start="836.399" dur="6.481">clemency, too. And we&amp;#39;re honored to be</text><text start="839.279" dur="5.281">joined by Pauliey&amp;#39;s father, Mark. And</text><text start="842.88" dur="4.319">Mark, if you would please come up and</text><text start="844.56" dur="5.719">say a few words. Thank you.</text><text start="847.199" dur="3.08">Thank you,</text><text start="854.959" dur="5.521">Mr. President, thank you for seeing us.</text><text start="858.56" dur="4.719">30 years ago, my daughter Paulie was</text><text start="860.48" dur="4.799">brutally taken from our family. A jury</text><text start="863.279" dur="4.24">heard the evidence, convicted her</text><text start="865.279" dur="5.36">killer, and imposed the strongest</text><text start="867.519" dur="5.12">sentence allowed under California law.</text><text start="870.639" dur="4.081">For three decades, our family lived with</text><text start="872.639" dur="5.361">the understanding that the justice</text><text start="874.72" dur="7.28">system&amp;#39;s decision would stand.</text><text start="878" dur="7.04">Today I stand before you outraged,</text><text start="882" dur="6">outraged that Governor Gavin Nuome</text><text start="885.04" dur="6.72">unilaterally erased that sentence and</text><text start="888" dur="6.16">547 more and commuted them to life</text><text start="891.76" dur="5.6">without parole without the consent of</text><text start="894.16" dur="5.28">victim&amp;#39;s families or the people of</text><text start="897.36" dur="4.96">California.</text><text start="899.44" dur="5.519">This decision was not made by a jury. It</text><text start="902.32" dur="6.079">was not approved by the voters.</text><text start="904.959" dur="5.041">It was made by one politician acting</text><text start="908.399" dur="3.601">alone.</text><text start="910" dur="4.959">While nothing can bring Polly back, her</text><text start="912" dur="5.36">life mattered. The pain inflicted on our</text><text start="914.959" dur="4.88">family was real and the pursuit of</text><text start="917.36" dur="5.52">justice should not become a political</text><text start="919.839" dur="5.841">exercise. I am here today to stand for</text><text start="922.88" dur="5.759">Paulie, for victim&amp;#39;s families across</text><text start="925.68" dur="5.92">California and for accountability in our</text><text start="928.639" dur="5.841">justice system. This is about more than</text><text start="931.6" dur="5.84">my family. This is about whether the</text><text start="934.48" dur="5.039">voices of crime victims matter. It&amp;#39;s</text><text start="937.44" dur="4.079">about whether one politician should have</text><text start="939.519" dur="4.961">the power to nullify the decisions of</text><text start="941.519" dur="5.841">judges, juries, and the citizens who</text><text start="944.48" dur="6.32">enacted these laws.</text><text start="947.36" dur="5.839">All to advance a political agenda. Mr.</text><text start="950.8" dur="4.88">President, thank you for hearing us.</text><text start="953.199" dur="5.481">Thank you for seeing us. Thank you very</text><text start="955.68" dur="3">much.</text><text start="970.24" dur="7.12">Mark went through, as you just heard, 30</text><text start="973.44" dur="7.68">years. 30 years. At the end of all of</text><text start="977.36" dur="7.039">that drama, it was just wiped out. It&amp;#39;s</text><text start="981.12" dur="5.68">probably just a political moment. So, I</text><text start="984.399" dur="4.961">want to thank you, Mark, and</text><text start="986.8" dur="4.56">uh just incredible what you&amp;#39;ve had to</text><text start="989.36" dur="4.159">endure. I saw your case. I watched it. I</text><text start="991.36" dur="3.919">watched you very closely the other day</text><text start="993.519" dur="5.201">in an interview. I said, &amp;quot;Boy, that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="995.279" dur="5.521">tough. That&amp;#39;s tough.&amp;quot;</text><text start="998.72" dur="5.6">The murders of these precious children</text><text start="1000.8" dur="7.039">are the worst nightmare of every mom and</text><text start="1004.32" dur="5.68">dad in America. Yet Gavin Newsome and</text><text start="1007.839" dur="4.881">the radical left look at these heinous</text><text start="1010" dur="4.399">acts and their sympathy is not for the</text><text start="1012.72" dur="4.4">children and their parents, but for the</text><text start="1014.399" dur="6.401">monsters who extinguished innocent young</text><text start="1017.12" dur="5.44">lives. Don&amp;#39;t understand it. Never did.</text><text start="1020.8" dur="5.119">I&amp;#39;ve seen it so much and I never</text><text start="1022.56" dur="6.8">understood it. And a lot of the media is</text><text start="1025.919" dur="5.12">with them for whatever reason. It&amp;#39;s not</text><text start="1029.36" dur="3.679">understandable.</text><text start="1031.039" dur="4.081">Under the Trump administration, we will</text><text start="1033.039" dur="5.201">never stop fighting to protect our</text><text start="1035.12" dur="4.799">nation&amp;#39;s children. And we will</text><text start="1038.24" dur="4.719">always take care. We&amp;#39;re just going to</text><text start="1039.919" dur="4.16">take care of our beautiful system of</text><text start="1042.959" dur="2.96">justice. We&amp;#39;re going to make it</text><text start="1044.079" dur="5.201">beautiful again. We&amp;#39;re going to bring</text><text start="1045.919" dur="6.241">justice for American families. There is</text><text start="1049.28" dur="5.2">no other choice. Also with us are the</text><text start="1052.16" dur="5.68">families of Detective Michael Davis and</text><text start="1054.48" dur="7.12">Deputy Sheriff Denny Oliver from the</text><text start="1057.84" dur="7.28">Plaster County Sheriff&amp;#39;s Office. In</text><text start="1061.6" dur="6.16">2014, we were involved. They were just</text><text start="1065.12" dur="4.559">involved in some it was a big a big</text><text start="1067.76" dur="5.52">thing happening</text><text start="1069.679" dur="5.441">in involved in a manhunt for an illegal</text><text start="1073.28" dur="3.84">alien criminal. A rough one that they</text><text start="1075.12" dur="5.2">were after for a long time. Rough rough</text><text start="1077.12" dur="6.24">rough. When they bravely approached the</text><text start="1080.32" dur="6.4">suspect&amp;#39;s vehicle, that illegal alien</text><text start="1083.36" dur="6.88">opened fire with a rifle and shot them</text><text start="1086.72" dur="6.72">both dead. Immediately dead. This is yet</text><text start="1090.24" dur="6.08">another monster Newsome spared. For what</text><text start="1093.44" dur="4.4">reason? I guess we know. I guess it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="1096.32" dur="2.96">politics. I don&amp;#39;t know how it&amp;#39;s good</text><text start="1097.84" dur="4.56">politics. I think it&amp;#39;s terrible</text><text start="1099.28" dur="5.44">politics. But that doesn&amp;#39;t matter.</text><text start="1102.4" dur="4.48">Should never have been done. I want to</text><text start="1104.72" dur="4.8">ask Detective Davis&amp;#39;s brother,</text><text start="1106.88" dur="4.88">Lieutenant Jason Davis, to come up and</text><text start="1109.52" dur="5.88">say a few words if you would. Thank you</text><text start="1111.76" dur="3.64">very much, please.</text><text start="1123.2" dur="4.4">Mr. President, on behalf of our family,</text><text start="1125.679" dur="3.681">I want to thank you and the Attorney</text><text start="1127.6" dur="4.079">General Blanch for your commitment to</text><text start="1129.36" dur="4.72">law and order. You have stood up for us</text><text start="1131.679" dur="4.161">victims from the beginning and uh we</text><text start="1134.08" dur="5.12">stand with you as well. Thank you very</text><text start="1135.84" dur="4.56">much, sir. My name is Jason Davis and as</text><text start="1139.2" dur="2.32">the president said, I&amp;#39;ve been a</text><text start="1140.4" dur="2.639">lieutenant with the Plaster County</text><text start="1141.52" dur="4.24">Sheriff&amp;#39;s Office where I&amp;#39;ve served as a</text><text start="1143.039" dur="4.481">law enforcement officer for 28 years. My</text><text start="1145.76" dur="3.279">family has a history of law enforcement</text><text start="1147.52" dur="3.44">service in the state of California,</text><text start="1149.039" dur="3.681">starting with my father who fulfilled</text><text start="1150.96" dur="4.959">his lifelong dream when he became a</text><text start="1152.72" dur="4.72">deputy sheriff in the early 80s.</text><text start="1155.919" dur="4.161">He was killed in the line of duty on</text><text start="1157.44" dur="4.479">October 24th, 1988, stopping drugs</text><text start="1160.08" dur="4">coming over the border of Mexico on a</text><text start="1161.919" dur="4.801">task force. Their helicopter went down</text><text start="1164.08" dur="4.88">when it hit power lines. He was killed</text><text start="1166.72" dur="4.319">instantly.</text><text start="1168.96" dur="5.28">My brother Michael and I followed in our</text><text start="1171.039" dur="6">f our father&amp;#39;s footsteps. I moved 500</text><text start="1174.24" dur="4.559">miles away from where I had grown up to</text><text start="1177.039" dur="4.161">Northern California to be with him,</text><text start="1178.799" dur="3.681">where we both served as deputy sheriffs</text><text start="1181.2" dur="3.599">with the Plaster County Sheriff&amp;#39;s</text><text start="1182.48" dur="4.48">Office. The greatest honor of my life</text><text start="1184.799" dur="5.801">was working patrol with my brother. He</text><text start="1186.96" dur="3.64">was my beat partner.</text><text start="1192.559" dur="4.961">26 years to the day after my dad had</text><text start="1195.039" dur="4.081">been killed, Michael was killed by Luis</text><text start="1197.52" dur="4.24">Brockamontis,</text><text start="1199.12" dur="4.64">who was in the United States illegally,</text><text start="1201.76" dur="4.72">went on a crime</text><text start="1203.76" dur="4.799">where he shot and killed Danny Oliver,</text><text start="1206.48" dur="4.8">uh, who contacted him in a hotel parking</text><text start="1208.559" dur="6.081">lot. His widow and daughter are here,</text><text start="1211.28" dur="5.279">Susan and Melissa. Thank you for coming.</text><text start="1214.64" dur="3.76">After he shot and killed Danny, he</text><text start="1216.559" dur="5.441">proceeded to carjack or attempt to</text><text start="1218.4" dur="6">carjack a hardcore street person who</text><text start="1222" dur="4.16">fought back. Brokammani shot him five</text><text start="1224.4" dur="5.04">times in the face. Miraculously, he</text><text start="1226.16" dur="5.2">survived. He then went on to carjack an</text><text start="1229.44" dur="3.599">innocent lady.</text><text start="1231.36" dur="3.28">After carjacking the innocent lady in</text><text start="1233.039" dur="3.361">Sacramento, he proceeded into the</text><text start="1234.64" dur="4.32">Plaster County territory where Michael</text><text start="1236.4" dur="4.32">got the call. Michael was a detective</text><text start="1238.96" dur="3.599">and had no business responding as a</text><text start="1240.72" dur="4.4">first responder or no obligation. He had</text><text start="1242.559" dur="4.561">business and he knew that Michael was a</text><text start="1245.12" dur="5.76">protector.</text><text start="1247.12" dur="5.12">Michael responded as a detective and was</text><text start="1250.88" dur="4.24">one of the first ones to encounter</text><text start="1252.24" dur="6.4">Brockam Montis. Circumstances played</text><text start="1255.12" dur="5.919">out. He was shot and killed instantly.</text><text start="1258.64" dur="4.32">Brokamontis went on the run where he was</text><text start="1261.039" dur="4.321">later captured by law enforcement. My</text><text start="1262.96" dur="7.079">agency as well as Sack County. Law</text><text start="1265.36" dur="4.679">enforcement wins. We have to.</text><text start="1270.799" dur="3.76">The man who murdered Michael was</text><text start="1272.88" dur="4.24">convicted by a jury of his peers and</text><text start="1274.559" dur="5.6">sentenced to death after receiving a</text><text start="1277.12" dur="4.799">full and fair fair trial,</text><text start="1280.159" dur="4.081">one that would be given to every citizen</text><text start="1281.919" dur="5.521">in this country.</text><text start="1284.24" dur="6.799">Yet, Governor Nuome chose to commute his</text><text start="1287.44" dur="6.4">sentence along with those 47 547 other</text><text start="1291.039" dur="4.64">inmates on death row, disregarding the</text><text start="1293.84" dur="4.079">victims or families and the will of the</text><text start="1295.679" dur="4.561">California voters.</text><text start="1297.919" dur="5.041">We had started to get closure. I had</text><text start="1300.24" dur="5.6">moved on. I could remember Michael</text><text start="1302.96" dur="5.36">outside of that incident. And Governor</text><text start="1305.84" dur="4.16">Newsome single-handedly ripped that</text><text start="1308.32" dur="4.16">band-aid off and opened that wound</text><text start="1310" dur="4.72">again. I have met with these families</text><text start="1312.48" dur="4.96">throughout the past two days and the</text><text start="1314.72" dur="4.48">past week. Their hearts are broken and</text><text start="1317.44" dur="3.28">mine breaks for theirs and Michael&amp;#39;s</text><text start="1319.2" dur="3.92">breaks for theirs because those were the</text><text start="1320.72" dur="3.6">people that Michael protected. Those</text><text start="1323.12" dur="2.799">were the people that Michael</text><text start="1324.32" dur="3.359">investigated</text><text start="1325.919" dur="3.841">so that our communities could be safe.</text><text start="1327.679" dur="4.321">And Governor Nuome under the cloak of</text><text start="1329.76" dur="5.039">darkness</text><text start="1332" dur="4.32">unilaterally makes a decision to commute</text><text start="1334.799" dur="4.081">the sentences of the most heinous</text><text start="1336.32" dur="4.8">criminals in our society.</text><text start="1338.88" dur="5.12">I am disgusted</text><text start="1341.12" dur="7.4">and frustrated.</text><text start="1344" dur="4.52">My brother did not die in vain.</text><text start="1351.679" dur="5.041">Mothers, there is nothing like a</text><text start="1353.52" dur="5.12">mother&amp;#39;s cry when she loses a child.</text><text start="1356.72" dur="5.199">As a law enforcement officer, I have</text><text start="1358.64" dur="7.36">delivered news many times to parents to</text><text start="1361.919" dur="5.681">a mom that your child is dead.</text><text start="1366" dur="3.679">usually</text><text start="1367.6" dur="5.68">through an accident or some other</text><text start="1369.679" dur="7.36">circumstance. I cannot fathom being told</text><text start="1373.28" dur="7.279">that my child was tortured, raped, duct</text><text start="1377.039" dur="6.721">taped for 10 hours by these animals. And</text><text start="1380.559" dur="5.841">then Gavin Newsome says, &amp;quot;Guess what? I</text><text start="1383.76" dur="5.2">got your back, inmates.</text><text start="1386.4" dur="5.36">I got your back.&amp;quot;</text><text start="1388.96" dur="5.36">You know what? Trump&amp;#39;s got our back. Our</text><text start="1391.76" dur="4.159">DOJ today has our back back. It is an</text><text start="1394.32" dur="3.76">honor to be here today. Even though I</text><text start="1395.919" dur="4.081">had zero desire to be here, I wanted to</text><text start="1398.08" dur="4.4">go and live a quiet life and raise my</text><text start="1400" dur="4.159">family.</text><text start="1402.48" dur="3.84">As a Christian, I&amp;#39;m called to forgive</text><text start="1404.159" dur="4.4">and I have forgiven the man who murdered</text><text start="1406.32" dur="4.32">my brother. But forgiveness does not</text><text start="1408.559" dur="4">eliminate accountability or erase</text><text start="1410.64" dur="3.76">consequences. Governor Nuomo</text><text start="1412.559" dur="3.201">unilaterally decided that Brock Lanis</text><text start="1414.4" dur="3.68">and these other inmates did not deserve</text><text start="1415.76" dur="6.159">the penalty that was imposed by their</text><text start="1418.08" dur="5.28">jurors by their jury by their peers.</text><text start="1421.919" dur="4.961">Nor does he believe the California</text><text start="1423.36" dur="6.24">voters who have twice California</text><text start="1426.88" dur="7.039">twice voted to impose a death penalty</text><text start="1429.6" dur="7.04">and had further uh on another measure</text><text start="1433.919" dur="5.361">voted to increase the expedit the</text><text start="1436.64" dur="5.36">quickness in which it happens</text><text start="1439.28" dur="5.36">and Governor N Governor Nuome in his</text><text start="1442" dur="4.159">morality clause decided ah you guys</text><text start="1444.64" dur="4.68">don&amp;#39;t know what you&amp;#39;re talking about I</text><text start="1446.159" dur="3.161">got this</text><text start="1450.08" dur="4.719">Michael lived his life protecting those</text><text start="1452" dur="5.12">who could not protect themselves. I ask</text><text start="1454.799" dur="4.721">that we never forget Michael or the</text><text start="1457.12" dur="4.559">victims or the families. Those were the</text><text start="1459.52" dur="5.12">people that Mike protected. I want to</text><text start="1461.679" dur="6.161">leave with a verse from Isaiah 5:20.</text><text start="1464.64" dur="5.039">Woe to those who call evil good and good</text><text start="1467.84" dur="4">evil.</text><text start="1469.679" dur="4.721">Who replace light for dark and dark for</text><text start="1471.84" dur="4.4">light. Governor Nuome, you made this</text><text start="1474.4" dur="3.6">move in the darkness because it was a</text><text start="1476.24" dur="4.72">political move that you thought would</text><text start="1478" dur="4.24">benefit yourself. But guess what? I</text><text start="1480.96" dur="6.36">don&amp;#39;t think it&amp;#39;s going to play out that</text><text start="1482.24" dur="5.08">way. Thank you very much and God bless.</text><text start="1497.279" dur="4.721">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you, Jason.</text><text start="1499.279" dur="4.4">It&amp;#39;s not easy to do for</text><text start="1502" dur="4">these people. This is very tough. I</text><text start="1503.679" dur="5.6">watch and it&amp;#39;s very tough. I&amp;#39;ve met so</text><text start="1506" dur="7.36">many others. Toughest thing. their whole</text><text start="1509.279" dur="6.961">lives have been turned around. We&amp;#39;re all</text><text start="1513.36" dur="5.679">also joined by the family of officer Gil</text><text start="1516.24" dur="5.039">Vega, 35-year-old veteran of Palm</text><text start="1519.039" dur="5.921">Springs Police Department and a father</text><text start="1521.279" dur="6.161">of eight. In 2016, Gil was two months</text><text start="1524.96" dur="5.68">away from retirement when he received a</text><text start="1527.44" dur="6.88">domestic disturbance call. Arriving at</text><text start="1530.64" dur="7.44">the scene, he was attacked by an armed</text><text start="1534.32" dur="6.4">gunman, a very vicious one with an AR-15</text><text start="1538.08" dur="5.599">who murdered Gil instantly and a fellow</text><text start="1540.72" dur="5.76">officer. I&amp;#39;d like to have his daughter,</text><text start="1543.679" dur="6.801">Gloria, come up say a few words about</text><text start="1546.48" dur="6.24">her great father, her hero, Officer Gil</text><text start="1550.48" dur="5.24">Vega. Thank you very much, Gloria. Thank</text><text start="1552.72" dur="3">you.</text><text start="1563.44" dur="5.599">Thank you for inviting us and letting me</text><text start="1566.24" dur="5.439">talk about my father. My father, Officer</text><text start="1569.039" dur="5.361">Jose Gil Vega, was a hardworking,</text><text start="1571.679" dur="4.801">loving, funny, and protective man. His</text><text start="1574.4" dur="4.56">smile could light up a room, and his</text><text start="1576.48" dur="4.96">laughter was contagious. He taught me</text><text start="1578.96" dur="4.8">that life would not always be easy, but</text><text start="1581.44" dur="4.64">no matter what challenges came my way, I</text><text start="1583.76" dur="4.72">should always make the best of them.</text><text start="1586.08" dur="3.839">For nearly 35 years, my dad proudly</text><text start="1588.48" dur="3.76">served the Palm Springs Police</text><text start="1589.919" dur="5.201">Department, the halls that I grew up in</text><text start="1592.24" dur="5.36">as well. Dedicating his life to protect</text><text start="1595.12" dur="5.28">others, he was twice recognized as</text><text start="1597.6" dur="4.559">officer of the year. But what truly made</text><text start="1600.4" dur="4.8">him special is the way he treated</text><text start="1602.159" dur="5.76">people. He can make someone laugh even</text><text start="1605.2" dur="5.04">while placing them under arrest. He</text><text start="1607.919" dur="4.24">treated everyone with dignity and</text><text start="1610.24" dur="3.76">respect regardless of their</text><text start="1612.159" dur="6">circumstances.</text><text start="1614" dur="6.96">On October 8th, 2016, just months before</text><text start="1618.159" dur="5.12">his retirement, my father was tragically</text><text start="1620.96" dur="5.599">killed in the line of duty while working</text><text start="1623.279" dur="5.041">overtime shift.</text><text start="1626.559" dur="4.321">After a large time of serving his</text><text start="1628.32" dur="5.359">community, he never got to enjoy his</text><text start="1630.88" dur="5.6">retirement he worked so hard to earn.</text><text start="1633.679" dur="6.081">And his partner Leslie Zerbney never was</text><text start="1636.48" dur="5.52">able to go home to her newborn daughter.</text><text start="1639.76" dur="5.519">My dad was more than a police officer.</text><text start="1642" dur="5.6">He was a loving father, a grandfather, a</text><text start="1645.279" dur="5.041">devoted public servant and a friend of</text><text start="1647.6" dur="5.84">many. I am incredibly proud to be his</text><text start="1650.32" dur="6">daughter and his love, sacrifice and</text><text start="1653.44" dur="6.839">legacy will stay with me forever. You</text><text start="1656.32" dur="3.959">know their lives mattered.</text><text start="1661.52" dur="3.639">Just thank you.</text><text start="1676.64" dur="5.6">Thank you, Gloria, very much.</text><text start="1679.679" dur="5.041">And in Officer Vega&amp;#39;s honor, I&amp;#39;m</text><text start="1682.24" dur="4.72">announcing today that I&amp;#39;ll contribute</text><text start="1684.72" dur="4.559">$5,000 to Trump account. That&amp;#39;s the</text><text start="1686.96" dur="5.12">maximum I&amp;#39;m allowed to give. Otherwise,</text><text start="1689.279" dur="4.321">Todd will have to come and arrest me.</text><text start="1692.08" dur="5.599">And I don&amp;#39;t like that. I wouldn&amp;#39;t like</text><text start="1693.6" dur="7.76">him for that. But uh I&amp;#39;m giving $5,000</text><text start="1697.679" dur="6.641">to his 17-year-old granddaughter,</text><text start="1701.36" dur="5.12">Angelina, who is also with us. Where&amp;#39;s</text><text start="1704.32" dur="5.16">Angelina? Hi, Angelina. Well,</text><text start="1706.48" dur="3">congratulations.</text><text start="1713.12" dur="3.84">Thank you, Barry.</text><text start="1715.039" dur="4.801">And Angelini, your grandfather is</text><text start="1716.96" dur="5.839">looking down right now on you both with</text><text start="1719.84" dur="5.76">great pride. Great pride.</text><text start="1722.799" dur="5.521">Thank you. Great job. Our nation</text><text start="1725.6" dur="6.24">grieavves for every law enforcement</text><text start="1728.32" dur="5.839">officer slain in the line of duty. That</text><text start="1731.84" dur="4.559">is why on day one of my administration,</text><text start="1734.159" dur="4.721">I signed an executive order directing</text><text start="1736.399" dur="4.4">Department of Justice to ensure that</text><text start="1738.88" dur="4.96">anyone who murders a member of law</text><text start="1740.799" dur="4.961">enforcement receives the death penalty.</text><text start="1743.84" dur="4.4">And I&amp;#39;m pleased to say that last year,</text><text start="1745.76" dur="5.76">police officer deaths in the line of</text><text start="1748.24" dur="5.439">duty plummeted to the lowest level in</text><text start="1751.52" dur="4.48">the history of our country.</text><text start="1753.679" dur="4.88">So, let me also recognize the other</text><text start="1756" dur="4.48">families with us whose loved ones were</text><text start="1758.559" dur="5.441">murdered by Newsome&amp;#39;s monsters,</text><text start="1760.48" dur="5.76">including the parents of Ball Bailey, an</text><text start="1764" dur="4.64">eight-year-old boy who was kidnapped by</text><text start="1766.24" dur="5.76">a former daycare employee, raped,</text><text start="1768.64" dur="5.919">strangled to death, and set on fire. The</text><text start="1772" dur="6.24">family of 26-year-old US Army veteran</text><text start="1774.559" dur="7.36">Sam her, who was shot twice in the head,</text><text start="1778.24" dur="5.679">and brutally dismembered.</text><text start="1781.919" dur="5.841">Hard to believe.</text><text start="1783.919" dur="6.64">The family of Daniel Hoover Nahara, a</text><text start="1787.76" dur="4.72">20- yearear-old firefighter with the US</text><text start="1790.559" dur="4.321">Forest Service who was killed by an</text><text start="1792.48" dur="4.799">arsonist. The family of Gabriel</text><text start="1794.88" dur="4.88">Fernandez, an 8-year-old boy, eight</text><text start="1797.279" dur="6.241">years old, think of that. Killed after</text><text start="1799.76" dur="7.68">months of severe abuse and torture.</text><text start="1803.52" dur="7.2">the family of officer Larry Lacier,</text><text start="1807.44" dur="5.599">35-year-old Marine veteran murdered by</text><text start="1810.72" dur="5.36">two armed robbery suspects, leaving</text><text start="1813.039" dur="6.88">behind a pregnant wife. I want to thank</text><text start="1816.08" dur="6.319">all of you and deepest sympathies to our</text><text start="1819.919" dur="5.921">entire nation and from our entire</text><text start="1822.399" dur="6.16">nation. In the Trump administration, we</text><text start="1825.84" dur="5.12">can find common ground with Democrats on</text><text start="1828.559" dur="4.48">many issues such as</text><text start="1830.96" dur="4.719">lowering the price of drugs where we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="1833.039" dur="4.721">done that at a record level, improving</text><text start="1835.679" dur="4.48">health care, and protecting the American</text><text start="1837.76" dur="6">worker. But when it comes to defending</text><text start="1840.159" dur="5.441">the lives and safety of American people,</text><text start="1843.76" dur="3.36">there can be no compromise. We&amp;#39;re not</text><text start="1845.6" dur="4.24">going to compromise. We&amp;#39;re going to take</text><text start="1847.12" dur="5.039">this right to the end. Law enforcement</text><text start="1849.84" dur="4.88">is not the enemy. the enemy are those</text><text start="1852.159" dur="6.081">who rape and murder our citizens and</text><text start="1854.72" dur="5.679">they deserve no mercy. For years now, we</text><text start="1858.24" dur="5.2">have watched the radical left commit one</text><text start="1860.399" dur="5.841">betrayal of justice and safety after</text><text start="1863.44" dur="5.44">another. Just days ago, a deranged</text><text start="1866.24" dur="4.799">homeless man with over 60 prior arrests.</text><text start="1868.88" dur="4.32">Think of that, 60 prior arrests, was</text><text start="1871.039" dur="4.801">charged with murdering a 62year-old</text><text start="1873.2" dur="6.24">woman in New York after radical left</text><text start="1875.84" dur="6.319">judges released him for custody.</text><text start="1879.44" dur="7.28">And uh this is like incredible. We</text><text start="1882.159" dur="7.441">released him to be uh his own guardian</text><text start="1886.72" dur="5.6">twice in the same month. Our opponents</text><text start="1889.6" dur="5.04">seek an America that empowers the most</text><text start="1892.32" dur="3.839">violent and dangerous elements and</text><text start="1894.64" dur="4.48">celebrates</text><text start="1896.159" dur="6.4">deviency and enables dysfunction and</text><text start="1899.12" dur="5.76">demands empathy for serial killers and</text><text start="1902.559" dur="4.561">criminals while hardworking citizens are</text><text start="1904.88" dur="5.12">treated with hatred and scorn and</text><text start="1907.12" dur="5.12">contempt. and nobody gets it. In the</text><text start="1910" dur="4.72">Trump administration, we believe in the</text><text start="1912.24" dur="5.279">exact opposite. We&amp;#39;re fighting to uplift</text><text start="1914.72" dur="5.199">the law-abiding and protect the most</text><text start="1917.519" dur="5.121">vulnerable, to reward hard work and</text><text start="1919.919" dur="4.801">decency, to defend the innocent, and to</text><text start="1922.64" dur="3.36">punish the guilty.</text><text start="1924.72" dur="2.72">You would think that would be just</text><text start="1926" dur="3.84">common sense, wouldn&amp;#39;t you? You would</text><text start="1927.44" dur="5.68">think everybody would be with us on</text><text start="1929.84" dur="6.88">that. But most people are. Every single</text><text start="1933.12" dur="5.279">day I&amp;#39;ve had the honor to serve as your</text><text start="1936.72" dur="4.799">president. It&amp;#39;s a great honor. There can</text><text start="1938.399" dur="6.16">be no greater honor. I&amp;#39;ll work to defeat</text><text start="1941.519" dur="5.28">those who would destroy everything you</text><text start="1944.559" dur="4.161">hold dear. And I&amp;#39;ll fight for your</text><text start="1946.799" dur="4.72">lives, your family, your safety, your</text><text start="1948.72" dur="5.199">dignity, and your freedom. Since I took</text><text start="1951.519" dur="4.321">office, we&amp;#39;ve achieved an unprecedented</text><text start="1953.919" dur="4.88">reduction in violent crime, including</text><text start="1955.84" dur="6.88">the largest drop ever the history of our</text><text start="1958.799" dur="6.401">country in the murder rate. And the</text><text start="1962.72" dur="6.24">lowest level in</text><text start="1965.2" dur="6.56">125 years is 1900. The year 1900. We had</text><text start="1968.96" dur="4.959">the best year. And I see cash in the</text><text start="1971.76" dur="5.919">audience. And I see you have a lot of</text><text start="1973.919" dur="7.681">talent sitting in that first row. And uh</text><text start="1977.679" dur="6.641">especially the wife of Todd Blanch,</text><text start="1981.6" dur="4.959">who&amp;#39;s a very special woman. He he&amp;#39;s not</text><text start="1984.32" dur="4.64">too easy to be with. I say he probably</text><text start="1986.559" dur="4.96">is. He&amp;#39;s a great man. He&amp;#39;s going to be</text><text start="1988.96" dur="5.04">He&amp;#39;s going to go down as a great man.</text><text start="1991.519" dur="4.801">Last year, there were more than 3,000</text><text start="1994" dur="3.919">fewer murders than before I took office.</text><text start="1996.32" dur="3.28">That&amp;#39;s a big statement. Federal law</text><text start="1997.919" dur="4.161">enforcement</text><text start="1999.6" dur="4.48">has arrested more than 1.2 million</text><text start="2002.08" dur="5.92">criminals under my administration.</text><text start="2004.08" dur="5.92">Violent crime arrests are up 90%.</text><text start="2008" dur="4.64">And we deployed the National Guard to</text><text start="2010" dur="5.12">restore law and order to Memphis, New</text><text start="2012.64" dur="5.2">Orleans, Washington DC, and crime is</text><text start="2015.12" dur="5.76">down more than 80%.</text><text start="2017.84" dur="4.88">Think of it in Washington DC. Every day</text><text start="2020.88" dur="3.84">I come to the office, somebody thanking</text><text start="2022.72" dur="4.4">me. It&amp;#39;s so because I remember two years</text><text start="2024.72" dur="5.92">ago it was a disaster.</text><text start="2027.12" dur="6.64">We average three murders a week, 150</text><text start="2030.64" dur="5.039">murders. And now you it&amp;#39;s very rare that</text><text start="2033.76" dur="5.84">we have anything like that happening.</text><text start="2035.679" dur="6">Crimes down some people say by 88%.</text><text start="2039.6" dur="3.84">It&amp;#39;s a safe city again. It&amp;#39;s a thriving</text><text start="2041.679" dur="3.36">city. Restaurants are opening. People</text><text start="2043.44" dur="2.88">are going out to dinner without any</text><text start="2045.039" dur="3.441">fear.</text><text start="2046.32" dur="4.16">What a difference it makes. I want to</text><text start="2048.48" dur="4.48">thank the many members of the police and</text><text start="2050.48" dur="5.119">law enforcement here today who have</text><text start="2052.96" dur="5.199">helped achieve those extraordinary gains</text><text start="2055.599" dur="4.161">in public safety. I see one of them</text><text start="2058.159" dur="4.24">right over there. Paul, would you please</text><text start="2059.76" dur="5.8">stand up? Border Patrol, my friend for a</text><text start="2062.399" dur="3.161">long time.</text><text start="2065.76" dur="5.599">Great job.</text><text start="2068.96" dur="6.879">Thanks as well to FBI Director Cash</text><text start="2071.359" dur="6.961">Patel, DEA Administrator Terry Cole,</text><text start="2075.839" dur="5.921">Dire Stand up fellows, will you please?</text><text start="2078.32" dur="7.4">You know, you deserve to stand up.</text><text start="2081.76" dur="3.96">Good. Hi, Terry.</text><text start="2087.76" dur="6.96">Director of the Bureau of Prisons, Billy</text><text start="2090.72" dur="6.48">Marshall. Billy, thank you, Billy.</text><text start="2094.72" dur="4.56">Thank you.</text><text start="2097.2" dur="6.12">US Attorney for the District of</text><text start="2099.28" dur="4.04">Columbia, Janine Piro.</text><text start="2104.64" dur="6.959">Thank you, Janine.</text><text start="2108" dur="5.76">Congressman Brandon Gil, a future star,</text><text start="2111.599" dur="5.161">I predict,</text><text start="2113.76" dur="3">right?</text><text start="2118" dur="6.4">the national president of the Fraternal</text><text start="2121.119" dur="6.321">Order of Police and a big supporter of</text><text start="2124.4" dur="5.28">me and people that really uh believe in</text><text start="2127.44" dur="4.399">you, the people in this room, Patrick</text><text start="2129.68" dur="5.399">Yo. Patrick, thank you. Thank you very</text><text start="2131.839" dur="3.24">much, Patrick.</text><text start="2135.119" dur="5.841">President of the California Fraternal</text><text start="2137.28" dur="8.36">Order of Police, Roger Hilton. Roger,</text><text start="2140.96" dur="4.68">thank you. Thank you.</text><text start="2145.839" dur="6.481">President of the Federal Law Enforcement</text><text start="2148.48" dur="7.8">Officers Association, Matthew Silverman.</text><text start="2152.32" dur="3.96">Matthew, thank you.</text><text start="2158.32" dur="6.08">And the former president of Crime</text><text start="2160.72" dur="6.879">Victims United, Nina Salerno. Nina,</text><text start="2164.4" dur="6.439">thank you very much.</text><text start="2167.599" dur="3.24">Thank you.</text><text start="2171.2" dur="4.72">Today, I&amp;#39;m announcing several major new</text><text start="2174" dur="3.92">actions to continue our progress</text><text start="2175.92" dur="4.32">combating violent crime and to ensure</text><text start="2177.92" dur="5.04">that the worst of the worst criminals</text><text start="2180.24" dur="4.56">are met with the retribution and</text><text start="2182.96" dur="4.72">punishment they deserve. You know, we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="2184.8" dur="4.96">gone 18 months now without one, it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="2187.68" dur="3.84">hard to believe actually, it almost I&amp;#39;d</text><text start="2189.76" dur="3.52">rather say a few got in because it</text><text start="2191.52" dur="4.079">sounds more believable, but this is a</text><text start="2193.28" dur="5.04">fact made by not us, but by other</text><text start="2195.599" dur="5.441">people. Not one person came through our</text><text start="2198.32" dur="5.279">southern border. Paul, not one for 18</text><text start="2201.04" dur="4.96">months, but one illegal alien, as we</text><text start="2203.599" dur="4.161">say, and that&amp;#39;s a record that probably</text><text start="2206" dur="4.48">will never be broken, but we&amp;#39;ll keep it</text><text start="2207.76" dur="4.48">going as long as we can. Already, the</text><text start="2210.48" dur="4.32">caravans have started, but we&amp;#39;re not</text><text start="2212.24" dur="4.8">letting them up, and Mexico better not</text><text start="2214.8" dur="4.88">let them up either. First, in a few</text><text start="2217.04" dur="4.72">moments, I will sign a presidential</text><text start="2219.68" dur="4.159">directive ordering the Department of</text><text start="2221.76" dur="5.04">Justice to seek the death penalty for</text><text start="2223.839" dur="4.641">child murderers as well as rapists and</text><text start="2226.8" dur="4.319">human traffickers who kill their</text><text start="2228.48" dur="4.56">victims. My order also directs the</text><text start="2231.119" dur="4.641">attorney general to expedite the</text><text start="2233.04" dur="4.64">execution of federal death sentences.</text><text start="2235.76" dur="5.599">Once juries have spoken, capital</text><text start="2237.68" dur="5.6">punishment will be swift and certain.</text><text start="2241.359" dur="4.081">I&amp;#39;m also directing the Department of</text><text start="2243.28" dur="4.559">Housing and Urban Development to compel</text><text start="2245.44" dur="5.04">public housing authorities to strengthen</text><text start="2247.839" dur="5.28">tenant screenings and make it easier to</text><text start="2250.48" dur="5.04">remove problematic tenants, of which</text><text start="2253.119" dur="4.561">people know who they are. Law-ab-bing</text><text start="2255.52" dur="4.88">families in need should not be forced to</text><text start="2257.68" dur="5.12">live beside dangerous criminals turning</text><text start="2260.4" dur="5.76">affordable housing into dens of violence</text><text start="2262.8" dur="5.76">and crime and horrible, horrible way to</text><text start="2266.16" dur="4.16">live. In addition, today I&amp;#39;m announcing</text><text start="2268.56" dur="6">that the Department of Justice will</text><text start="2270.32" dur="6.48">award nearly $150 million to new public</text><text start="2274.56" dur="4.72">safety grants to help hire more than</text><text start="2276.8" dur="6.24">1,000 additional sworn law enforcement</text><text start="2279.28" dur="6.16">officers and speed up response times to</text><text start="2283.04" dur="5.039">reports of domestic violence and sexual</text><text start="2285.44" dur="5.88">assault nationwide.</text><text start="2288.079" dur="3.241">Thank you.</text><text start="2292.96" dur="4.96">Thank you very much.</text><text start="2295.599" dur="4.801">And finally, at my request, Congressman</text><text start="2297.92" dur="4.8">Brandon Gil has just introduced a new</text><text start="2300.4" dur="4.48">bill to strengthen the death penalty in</text><text start="2302.72" dur="4.72">America. And it&amp;#39;s going to be much</text><text start="2304.88" dur="4.4">different than it was in the past. Uh</text><text start="2307.44" dur="5.679">it&amp;#39;s going to be strong. It&amp;#39;s going to</text><text start="2309.28" dur="7.68">be swift. The Just Punishment for Murder</text><text start="2313.119" dur="6.081">Act will codify many aspects of today&amp;#39;s</text><text start="2316.96" dur="4.639">directive along with my executive order</text><text start="2319.2" dur="4.56">on capital punishment for killers of law</text><text start="2321.599" dur="4.321">enforcement. and it will expand the</text><text start="2323.76" dur="4.56">policy to ensure that illegal alien</text><text start="2325.92" dur="4.96">murderers are likewise sentenced to</text><text start="2328.32" dur="4.56">death. And I&amp;#39;m calling on Congress to</text><text start="2330.88" dur="3.52">send me that bill without delay. And I</text><text start="2332.88" dur="6.199">will sign it, Brandon, very, very</text><text start="2334.4" dur="4.679">quickly. Okay. Thank you very much.</text><text start="2340.16" dur="4.959">And the ultimate</text><text start="2342.16" dur="6">crimes deserve the ultimate punishment.</text><text start="2345.119" dur="6">This age-old wisdom has been a principle</text><text start="2348.16" dur="5.04">of virtually every society throughout</text><text start="2351.119" dur="4.321">history. at least every successful</text><text start="2353.2" dur="4.24">society. And under the Trump</text><text start="2355.44" dur="4.96">administration, we are bringing it back.</text><text start="2357.44" dur="5.76">And we will not stop in our pursuit of</text><text start="2360.4" dur="4.88">justice. We will not yield. And we just</text><text start="2363.2" dur="4.879">won&amp;#39;t yield to the communists, to</text><text start="2365.28" dur="4.64">criminals, to horrible people, people</text><text start="2368.079" dur="4.641">that want to destroy our country. People</text><text start="2369.92" dur="4.48">that really desire to just destroy our</text><text start="2372.72" dur="4.24">country.</text><text start="2374.4" dur="4.24">And I guess they know it. Many of them</text><text start="2376.96" dur="4.08">do. We&amp;#39;re not going to let it happen.</text><text start="2378.64" dur="4.4">will not waver in our commitment to</text><text start="2381.04" dur="4.72">these families and we will fight, fight,</text><text start="2383.04" dur="5.52">fight and we will make America safer and</text><text start="2385.76" dur="4.4">stronger and greater than ever before.</text><text start="2388.56" dur="4.799">And I want to just thank everybody in</text><text start="2390.16" dur="5.199">this audience. You have so many I know</text><text start="2393.359" dur="3.681">so many are incredible. These are</text><text start="2395.359" dur="4.161">incredible people. You&amp;#39;re the people</text><text start="2397.04" dur="5.12">that keep us all safe. You&amp;#39;re</text><text start="2399.52" dur="4.319">incredible, beautiful people. And I want</text><text start="2402.16" dur="3.52">to thank you very much. It&amp;#39;s an honor to</text><text start="2403.839" dur="5.841">be your president. Thank you everybody.</text><text start="2405.68" dur="4">God bless you all. Thank you.</text><text start="2422.217" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [applause]</text></transcript>